 189+ 0286              ; Guest RAM backing access
 190+ 0286              ;
 191+ 0286              ; Guest RAM allocation starts at NeoGS physical page 44h.
 192+ 0286              ; Guest byte address maps linearly to physical offset 110000h + guest address.
 193+ 0286              ; WIN3 is a permanently reserved bank aperture; its current page is volatile.
 194+ 0286              ; These routines do not restore WIN3's previous page because the page port is
 195+ 0286              ; write-only and WIN3 is owned exclusively by this memory backend.
 196+ 0286              ;
 197+ 0286              ; Entry address: x86_phys_addr = low, middle, high-nibble.
 198+ 0286              ; Read returns byte in A, carry clear. Non-RAM overlay regions return carry.
 199+ 0286              ; Write takes byte in A, carry clear on success; non-RAM returns carry.
